cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its evidence, please cite it as below."
title: "dense-uav-ops: a research simulator for the safety–capacity frontier of dense, mixed-equipage UAS traffic"
abstract: >-
  Open research software that simulates dense low-altitude UAS traffic with mixed
  equipage, delayed and bounded-error surveillance, and configurable assumptions
  about other aircraft's motion, and measures attributable separation risk against
  delivered service. Includes a NASA DAIDALUS baseline, optional learned rankers,
  declared and resumable experiment campaigns, and validated historical evidence.
  Results are simulation evidence under stated assumptions, not operational safety
  or capacity claims.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tripathi
    given-names: Vibhu
repository-code: "https://github.com/not-vibhu/dense-uav-ops"
license: MIT
version: 0.5.0
keywords:
  - unmanned aircraft systems
  - UTM
  - tactical deconfliction
  - airspace capacity
  - detect and avoid
  - simulation
  - DAIDALUS
